WEBVTT

00:22.605 --> 00:25.108
Auroras are the light created when Earth,

00:25.692 --> 00:27.318
forever unable to reach the Sun,

00:28.069 --> 00:33.033
draws in minute traces of solar plasma
with the pull of its magnetic field.

00:40.457 --> 00:42.709
Perhaps this dazzling, mesmerizing light

00:43.877 --> 00:47.172
is but a tragic, fleeting illusion

00:47.672 --> 00:50.008
born from the Earth's yearning
for the Sun,

00:50.091 --> 00:52.844
fooling it into believing
that a mere brush with the Sun

00:53.636 --> 00:56.014
has brought the two closer.

01:14.491 --> 01:15.867
On that night,

01:17.118 --> 01:19.204
for the first time ever,

01:19.871 --> 01:22.582
I desperately hoped
my delusion would become a reality.

01:26.044 --> 01:28.713
But Earth can never reach the Sun,

01:29.380 --> 01:32.842
and auroras do not appear
in the skies above Seoul.

01:50.235 --> 01:51.444
Mr. Joo Ho-jin,

01:52.237 --> 01:53.321
let's head back now.

01:54.239 --> 01:56.616
We can stay and watch until it disappears.

01:57.492 --> 02:00.578
That's all right.
I don't want to watch it disappear.

02:03.706 --> 02:05.917
We saw it together, as promised.

02:06.417 --> 02:07.752
That's good enough.

02:27.897 --> 02:29.190
It's gone.

02:32.777 --> 02:34.696
I thought I told you to head inside.

02:35.196 --> 02:37.490
Did my threat to kill you earlier
freak you out?

02:38.575 --> 02:39.826
It did at first,

02:40.326 --> 02:43.121
but I'm waiting here now
to find out why it ever happened.

02:43.204 --> 02:46.291
All you need to do is act
like you didn't hear what you heard.

02:47.333 --> 02:48.168
That's all?

02:48.751 --> 02:50.003
But I'm an awful liar.

02:52.130 --> 02:55.508
I just don't want anyone to know
that the wedding's off.

02:56.342 --> 02:58.428
Well, everyone will find out soon enough.

03:01.389 --> 03:02.307
Fancy a fight?

03:02.891 --> 03:05.643
Excuse me. You're the one
who started it with your death threat.

03:10.148 --> 03:13.234
You're not scared of my threat.
You're having a blast teasing me.

03:13.735 --> 03:16.738
I used to be an athlete,
so I have great reflexes.

03:17.363 --> 03:18.823
This phone isn't dead either.

03:19.324 --> 03:20.283
He's calling again.

03:20.825 --> 03:23.244
Take it
before I accidentally answer again.

03:28.082 --> 03:29.083
Did he cheat on you?

03:30.251 --> 03:33.588
Seems like the guy's begging you
to take him back, but don't.

03:34.339 --> 03:36.257
There's no going back from cheating.

03:38.259 --> 03:39.344
Is that right?

03:40.011 --> 03:42.180
Is there no going back if someone cheats?

03:48.269 --> 03:49.437
Jin-suk.

03:50.021 --> 03:51.773
I can't marry you.

03:52.315 --> 03:53.233
I cheated on you.

03:55.151 --> 03:56.653
So don't ever call me again.

03:57.237 --> 03:58.488
We're over.

04:02.283 --> 04:05.036
You are the one… who cheated?

04:05.119 --> 04:06.829
I'm going to start right now.

04:07.538 --> 04:08.373
Cheating.

04:18.341 --> 04:19.425
It's stuck, isn't it?

04:19.509 --> 04:21.219
This has happened to me before

04:21.719 --> 04:22.971
with old hotels in Europe.

04:24.514 --> 04:26.808
If you keep twisting,
the lock will pop open.

04:30.061 --> 04:31.062
You must be tired.

04:31.854 --> 04:33.731
Today's shoot ran a bit long.

04:34.399 --> 04:35.900
I get puffy when I'm tired.

04:36.401 --> 04:38.486
I guess today's shoot was a tough one.

04:39.320 --> 04:40.154
A bit.

04:41.447 --> 04:45.827
It was cold, no sign of the aurora,
and just awkward silence between us.

04:46.411 --> 04:48.871
So we just stoked the fire
and roasted things.

04:48.955 --> 04:51.416
We roasted potatoes and marshmallows.

04:51.916 --> 04:54.002
I'm still full from eating it all myself.

04:54.085 --> 04:57.380
Why'd you eat all of it by yourself?
Was he being prickly again?

04:58.131 --> 04:58.965
No.

04:59.465 --> 05:02.385
Hiro's watching what he eats
because he gains weight easily.

05:02.885 --> 05:04.846
Nanami gave me a little heads-up.

05:05.805 --> 05:06.764
Right.

05:06.848 --> 05:09.350
She also said that Hiro's been cranky

05:09.434 --> 05:13.855
because he's sensitive to the cold,
has dry eyes, and all sorts of allergies.

05:14.355 --> 05:16.983
When we were holding hands,
I noticed they were ice-cold.

05:17.483 --> 05:18.901
Maybe he has poor circulation.

05:20.028 --> 05:21.904
You held hands with…

05:25.033 --> 05:26.743
Why won't this thing open?

05:26.826 --> 05:28.870
So I'm going to look out for him
from now on.

05:30.663 --> 05:34.042
That's why I ate
all the marshmallows today.

05:34.667 --> 05:36.586
He smiled, so I guess he was grateful.

05:36.669 --> 05:40.757
I think I get why they call him
the Prince of Romance now.

05:41.424 --> 05:43.384
He's pretty cute when he smiles.

05:43.468 --> 05:45.803
Why won't this darn thing open?

05:47.221 --> 05:49.640
-Is it stuck?
-Just leave it to me.

05:50.141 --> 05:52.727
And he has these dimples when he smiles.

05:54.145 --> 05:54.979
Where?

05:57.440 --> 05:59.150
If you look closely, right here.

06:00.860 --> 06:04.405
Can you really call it a dimple
if you have to look closely to spot it?

06:08.368 --> 06:09.786
Why won't this open?

06:09.869 --> 06:11.412
Did someone jam it on purpose?

06:17.126 --> 06:18.127
It's open!

06:18.211 --> 06:19.879
Thank goodness!

06:21.089 --> 06:22.548
I banged my head…

06:23.591 --> 06:26.135
-You should go inside and rest.
-Thank you.

06:27.053 --> 06:27.887
By the way,

06:27.970 --> 06:31.474
Hiro says his favorite Korean food
is japchae with lots of mushrooms.

06:31.974 --> 06:33.851
Can you teach me how to make it?

06:34.685 --> 06:35.520
I don't know how.

06:35.603 --> 06:37.063
I thought you were a good cook.

06:37.146 --> 06:38.272
I've never made it.

06:39.482 --> 06:42.443
-I'll just look it up on YouTube.
-Look it up. Sure.

06:42.944 --> 06:44.654
Go on in and rest. What was it again?

06:44.737 --> 06:46.114
Earlier, you said…

06:46.781 --> 06:48.741
Marshmallows. You said you ate a lot.

06:48.825 --> 06:50.284
Your face is all puffy.

06:59.001 --> 07:00.878
So who will you cheat on him with?

07:03.423 --> 07:06.801
Any unmarried guy
over the age of 20 would be fine.

07:08.803 --> 07:11.139
How would that be fine?
That could be anyone.

07:11.222 --> 07:13.766
I'm not looking for someone
I'd actually fall for.

07:14.725 --> 07:17.812
So if you're not looking
for a good guy to move on with,

07:18.312 --> 07:19.439
why must you cheat?

07:20.022 --> 07:21.899
Because it has to be irreversible.

07:22.483 --> 07:25.236
That way, I won't be able
to go back to him no matter what.

07:28.030 --> 07:30.491
Still, you can't just do that with anyone.

07:31.033 --> 07:33.870
Not only would it be dangerous,
but it would also be depraved!

07:35.788 --> 07:38.124
So what? Should it be with someone I know?

07:39.375 --> 07:40.626
To be safe and dignified?

07:42.962 --> 07:44.213
Someone you know? Who?

07:44.881 --> 07:45.965
Wait a minute.

07:46.549 --> 07:48.634
You don't mean Ho-jin, do you?

07:49.594 --> 07:50.428
Do you?

07:50.511 --> 07:54.474
Sure, you seem to have lost your marbles,
but you're not that far gone, are you?

08:00.229 --> 08:01.856
I can't with him.

08:02.356 --> 08:03.816
He doesn't meet the criteria.

08:04.817 --> 08:05.902
The criteria?

08:07.111 --> 08:09.614
I told you it can't be someone
I might really fall for.

08:10.114 --> 08:11.407
Which means

08:11.991 --> 08:14.202
it can't be someone I once liked either.

08:16.954 --> 08:18.039
There was a time

08:18.539 --> 08:20.333
when I liked Joo Ho-jin.

08:24.587 --> 08:29.258
CAN THIS LOVE BE TRANSLATED?

08:33.846 --> 08:35.431
Why won't they let us in?

08:35.515 --> 08:37.934
I thought you said you understood English.

08:38.017 --> 08:39.060
You're useless!

08:39.143 --> 08:42.188
I'm telling you,
they have weird accents I can't make out.

08:42.271 --> 08:44.148
Even Ji-sun didn't understand.

08:44.232 --> 08:46.943
Ho-jin's on the phone now,
so we'll find out soon.

08:47.443 --> 08:50.530
They say we told the Ministry of Tourism
we're shooting tomorrow.

08:50.613 --> 08:51.822
Tomorrow?

08:53.115 --> 08:55.159
Producer Kim's trouble until the very end!

08:55.243 --> 08:56.369
That pain in the ass.

08:56.452 --> 09:00.206
They said the park office is inside
and suggested we talk to them directly.

09:00.289 --> 09:03.626
We need to shoot before the park opens
and gets too crowded.

09:03.709 --> 09:07.421
-Should we go plead with them?
-Yes. Mr. Joo, please come with us.

09:08.130 --> 09:09.590
Go let the cast know.

09:13.094 --> 09:16.847
Can you let Mu-hee know that the shoot
will be delayed by at least 30 minutes?

09:16.931 --> 09:18.099
Sure, will do.

09:18.182 --> 09:19.016
Thanks.

09:26.857 --> 09:29.527
There was a time when I liked Joo Ho-jin.

09:31.195 --> 09:32.738
Things sure are complicated.

10:14.905 --> 10:16.198
What are you doing there?

10:18.242 --> 10:21.203
She was a dying zombie yesterday,
but I guess she's been revived.

10:25.833 --> 10:27.126
Taking pictures again?

10:32.632 --> 10:34.258
You shouldn't wander the forest alone.

10:34.342 --> 10:36.344
They say Canadian forests have bears.

10:37.094 --> 10:38.012
Bear…

10:38.095 --> 10:39.513
How do you say "bear" again?

10:41.140 --> 10:41.974
Fu…

10:43.684 --> 10:45.311
Fu Bao!

10:45.853 --> 10:46.687
Bear!

10:49.065 --> 10:49.899
What's that?

10:49.982 --> 10:52.109
You know, bears!

10:52.193 --> 10:53.194
You'll be eaten!

10:55.780 --> 10:56.656
Oh, bear?

10:57.281 --> 10:59.450
Yes, bear. That's it.

11:00.951 --> 11:02.662
That was nothing like a bear.

11:03.162 --> 11:05.998
Plus, you're more dangerous than a bear.
You're a zombie.

11:08.167 --> 11:12.004
Your hands are really red.
You definitely have poor circulation.

11:13.089 --> 11:13.923
Freezing, right?

11:15.091 --> 11:16.133
What are you doing?

11:16.217 --> 11:18.386
You should really carry around
some heat packs.

11:19.595 --> 11:20.680
Want some of mine?

11:31.607 --> 11:32.608
Here. They're warm.

11:35.152 --> 11:37.530
I stuck a bunch of them on me,
so I'll be fine.

11:40.658 --> 11:41.742
And eat this.

11:42.284 --> 11:43.119
It's

11:43.994 --> 11:44.954
sugar-free.

11:45.496 --> 11:47.331
No sugar. No fat.

11:48.332 --> 11:49.375
Candy?

11:49.458 --> 11:51.043
-This is ame?
-Yes, ame.

11:52.169 --> 11:54.547
So candy is "ame" in Japanese?

11:56.257 --> 11:57.925
We may not speak the same language,

11:58.008 --> 12:02.304
but things that feel warm or taste sweet
are surely universal.

12:07.852 --> 12:11.355
Nanami said that you glowed
when you were with me.

12:12.940 --> 12:15.192
Since we're alone, I can check for sure.

12:15.693 --> 12:18.195
One can sense these things
despite not speaking the same language.

12:27.329 --> 12:29.039
Now, if you have something to say,

12:29.957 --> 12:31.667
please say it into this.

12:44.388 --> 12:45.556
Glowing.

12:50.770 --> 12:52.229
Glowing.

12:54.106 --> 12:55.608
"Glowing"?

12:56.692 --> 12:57.610
What is?

13:09.205 --> 13:11.040
So this is what was glowing.

13:14.543 --> 13:16.670
My earrings? What about them?

13:26.931 --> 13:29.308
Man, that was close.

13:29.391 --> 13:31.977
Imagine if I'd asked her if she likes me.

13:32.061 --> 13:33.395
What would've happened?

13:37.399 --> 13:39.485
I don't like you!

13:58.254 --> 14:00.339
So there really are bears around here.

14:02.132 --> 14:04.218
Bear! You'll be eaten!

14:24.321 --> 14:25.531
Don't things look good?

14:39.378 --> 14:42.047
-What a relief!
-Man, that was stressful.

14:44.091 --> 14:46.677
Mu-hee, thank you so much.

14:46.760 --> 14:48.304
Do Ra-mi is the best!

14:48.387 --> 14:49.513
Thank you.

14:49.597 --> 14:51.056
Mu-hee, you should stay here.

14:51.140 --> 14:53.601
Once the gates open,
we'll all drive up here anyway.

14:53.684 --> 14:55.436
-Let's go, Ho-jin.
-Sure.

15:01.191 --> 15:03.027
Stay here.

15:07.406 --> 15:10.284
You promised to teach me basic Japanese.

15:10.868 --> 15:12.578
Ho-jin, don't go back down.

15:12.661 --> 15:13.996
Just stay here with me.

15:18.584 --> 15:19.960
Hey, I'll wait here too.

15:20.836 --> 15:22.129
All right, then.

15:30.888 --> 15:31.805
So…

15:33.849 --> 15:35.851
you wanted me to teach you Japanese?

15:37.770 --> 15:40.105
No, that was just…

15:43.233 --> 15:45.653
You said you were afraid of her.
I was protecting you.

15:47.112 --> 15:48.572
Thanks for looking out for me,

15:49.073 --> 15:51.617
but I'm not so tuned in to her
that this feels awkward.

15:52.159 --> 15:53.577
Do you see me

15:54.119 --> 15:56.664
as some lovesick teen
pining over unrequited love?

15:56.747 --> 15:57.915
So it's not that bad?

15:58.749 --> 16:02.878
I was worried you had been restless,
tossing and turning every night.

16:09.593 --> 16:10.427
Wait up.

16:14.682 --> 16:16.600
-Isn't the Sun in your eyes?
-It is.

16:16.684 --> 16:17.643
How about now?

16:20.771 --> 16:21.605
Careful.

16:22.147 --> 16:23.273
Walk this way.

16:25.234 --> 16:26.986
Canadians seem

16:28.028 --> 16:30.197
so warm and friendly.

16:31.407 --> 16:34.576
Maybe it's because they live
somewhere quiet and with fresh air?

16:36.036 --> 16:37.246
The park isn't open yet.

16:38.789 --> 16:41.959
Once it opens, it'll be crowded and loud.

16:43.377 --> 16:46.130
You've been here before too?

16:46.964 --> 16:50.175
Yes, as a kid with my family,
when we lived in the US.

16:50.968 --> 16:53.178
Further that way,
there's a small waterfall.

16:53.721 --> 16:54.555
A waterfall?

16:55.514 --> 16:57.516
It's not far. About a 20-minute walk.

16:58.684 --> 17:00.936
-Do you want to see it? Want to go?
-I do.

17:07.192 --> 17:08.027
Careful.

17:18.120 --> 17:18.954
What is it?

17:19.580 --> 17:22.291
Sorry. I can't find it.
It must not be this way.

17:22.791 --> 17:26.336
With your sense of direction,
of course you wouldn't find the way.

17:26.837 --> 17:29.339
If we keep wandering, we'll be late.
Let's turn back.

17:29.840 --> 17:31.925
No way you're taking the lead. Follow me.

17:32.009 --> 17:34.553
But… it's this way.

17:38.307 --> 17:39.516
Or maybe it is this way.

17:44.063 --> 17:45.606
What a view.

17:50.277 --> 17:53.363
There must be a waterfall
somewhere on that mountain, right?

17:54.698 --> 17:55.783
There definitely

17:56.492 --> 17:57.993
was one.

17:59.703 --> 18:00.829
Is that it?

18:02.498 --> 18:03.332
Where?

18:03.415 --> 18:05.334
Right there. Can't you see the waterfall?

18:06.460 --> 18:08.712
There. It's just over there.

18:08.796 --> 18:09.671
I don't see it--

18:09.755 --> 18:11.006
Just say that you see it.

18:11.507 --> 18:12.674
Sure, let's say I do.

18:14.468 --> 18:16.470
Then this isn't a lake. It's a waterfall.

18:20.099 --> 18:22.101
Wow, a waterfall.

18:22.184 --> 18:25.145
If you insist
that any falling water is a waterfall,

18:25.229 --> 18:27.356
tap water would also be a waterfall.

18:28.190 --> 18:30.734
Okay, sure. This is a waterfall. Yep.

18:32.111 --> 18:34.905
No one in the world
would call this a waterfall.

18:35.572 --> 18:36.782
Then this is a waterfall

18:38.450 --> 18:39.993
that only you and I know about.

18:41.161 --> 18:43.330
Fine. Let's say it's a waterfall.

18:45.749 --> 18:47.167
Wow.

18:47.668 --> 18:49.586
The waterfall's nice and cool.

19:27.207 --> 19:28.834
Do Ra-mi made me do it.

19:29.334 --> 19:31.128
She made me threaten you.

19:32.504 --> 19:34.464
I told you to watch out.

19:46.310 --> 19:47.561
Cha Mu…

19:51.523 --> 19:53.567
Thanks for an amazing shoot in Canada!

20:01.742 --> 20:02.910
-Nice.
-You're good.

20:02.993 --> 20:05.287
But now we have to aim here.

20:05.370 --> 20:07.623
Bam! Yeah, hit it head-on.

20:07.706 --> 20:08.916
Wow, you did so well!

20:08.999 --> 20:11.168
She sure looks fine after threatening me.

20:14.046 --> 20:16.590
That's it! Do you get it now?

20:18.258 --> 20:20.552
They can't communicate,
but they're strategizing?

20:21.261 --> 20:22.095
-"Nigiru"?
-Yeah.

20:22.179 --> 20:23.222
What does that mean?

20:24.306 --> 20:25.349
Attention, everyone!

20:26.600 --> 20:28.560
In a desperate moment of crisis,

20:28.644 --> 20:31.939
I bring to you the elite warrior duo,
here to avenge the crew.

20:32.022 --> 20:33.357
Please come in!

20:45.827 --> 20:48.497
All right, then. Let's resume the match!

20:48.580 --> 20:49.998
Let's crush them!

21:12.145 --> 21:13.689
Great job!

21:14.564 --> 21:15.983
How did he even manage that?

21:16.066 --> 21:17.609
We have one player left!

21:18.110 --> 21:24.449
Joo Ho-jin!

21:24.533 --> 21:26.326
-Go on.
-Joo Ho-jin!

21:27.286 --> 21:29.871
-You can do it!
-Just push that one out of the way.

21:30.372 --> 21:32.499
If it stops in the middle, we win.

21:33.500 --> 21:34.626
You've got this.

21:35.669 --> 21:37.921
-Let's go!
-Let's win this thing!

22:18.337 --> 22:20.339
It's okay. We did good.

22:20.422 --> 22:21.923
It's okay.

22:22.007 --> 22:24.176
You did great.

22:25.385 --> 22:27.179
It's okay.

22:27.262 --> 22:29.765
Joo Ho-jin!

22:29.848 --> 22:31.475
Joo Ho-jin!

22:43.528 --> 22:44.863
Joo Ho-jin!

22:45.364 --> 22:48.700
-Joo Ho-jin! Joo…
-Joo Ho-jin!

22:48.784 --> 22:49.951
Joo Ho-jin!

22:50.619 --> 22:51.453
Sorry?

22:52.079 --> 22:52.996
Everyone.

22:53.497 --> 22:56.708
Hiro says that,
to celebrate the crew's curling victory,

22:56.792 --> 22:58.210
drinks are on him tonight!

23:00.879 --> 23:05.550
Hiro!

23:05.634 --> 23:09.471
Hiro!

23:09.554 --> 23:11.890
Thank you!

23:13.058 --> 23:14.726
Thank you, everyone!

23:24.986 --> 23:28.824
He said he hated losing,
but he doesn't seem too mad about it.

23:30.325 --> 23:32.202
You said you hate losing,

23:32.285 --> 23:34.704
but you don't seem too mad about losing.

23:35.205 --> 23:37.416
It was so much fun
that I didn't mind losing.

23:39.418 --> 23:41.753
He said that he had a lot of fun.

24:08.864 --> 24:10.240
Thank you for your hard work.

24:16.580 --> 24:19.082
You didn't like Ms. Cha Mu-hee at first,

24:19.166 --> 24:21.626
but while filming,
you seem to have changed your mind.

24:22.127 --> 24:22.961
No.

24:23.462 --> 24:26.590
I hate that zombie even more now.

24:28.049 --> 24:30.469
Thanks to her, I've become a joke.

24:33.889 --> 24:37.350
-Joo Ho-jin!
-Knock it off.

24:40.520 --> 24:45.901
Could I ask you for one more favor?

24:47.903 --> 24:50.947
Mr. Joo, are you looking
to get married at all?

24:51.698 --> 24:52.532
I'm sorry?

24:53.283 --> 24:56.161
We're working on a dating show,

24:56.244 --> 24:58.163
and, Mr. Joo, I really,

24:58.663 --> 25:02.375
really… really want you
as one of our noncelebrity contestants.

25:04.836 --> 25:06.630
I don't think I can help you there.

25:07.797 --> 25:09.174
So it's a no after all.

25:09.883 --> 25:13.929
I asked Producer Shin about it recently,
and she said you'd say no.

25:14.012 --> 25:16.723
I hear you've liked someone
for a very long time.

25:17.599 --> 25:20.435
That's what Ji-sun told me.
Is that not true?

25:25.315 --> 25:27.275
Is… it not?

25:29.110 --> 25:30.612
Goodness me.

25:31.154 --> 25:32.656
I should call home.

25:33.406 --> 25:34.574
Excuse me a moment.

25:35.617 --> 25:37.118
Why did I bring up his private life…

25:46.503 --> 25:47.796
Mic test.

25:47.879 --> 25:49.965
Can I have your attention, please?

25:52.425 --> 25:55.720
Thank you all for your work on this shoot,
despite the cold weather.

26:00.350 --> 26:03.103
I have another gig in Korea,

26:03.186 --> 26:06.690
so I'll be leaving before the rest of you.

26:06.773 --> 26:10.569
I'll see you all soon in Italy.
Thank you again.

26:29.963 --> 26:31.381
You're heading back already?

26:32.007 --> 26:34.676
You can stay longer.
We just need to leave by 8:00 tomorrow.

26:35.844 --> 26:37.470
No, let's call it a night.

26:38.263 --> 26:40.932
Okay. Wait here. I'll get the car.

27:55.882 --> 27:59.135
Why is my movie suddenly playing?

28:16.152 --> 28:17.070
Hey!

28:17.570 --> 28:18.613
Did I surprise you?

28:19.114 --> 28:19.948
It's me.

28:22.909 --> 28:23.993
Why are you so shocked?

28:25.829 --> 28:28.248
You've been talking to him
about me a lot lately.

28:30.542 --> 28:31.835
Whatever. Get lost.

28:32.335 --> 28:34.713
You kissed him thanks to me.
Now you're acting coy?

28:41.678 --> 28:42.929
Follow me.

28:43.430 --> 28:45.098
I'll show you something fun.

29:16.880 --> 29:18.089
Mr. Joo Ho-jin!

29:18.173 --> 29:19.174
Now,

29:19.674 --> 29:23.011
I'm going to ask you some questions
Cha Mu-hee wants answers to.

29:25.263 --> 29:28.141
You know she's leaving first tomorrow.
Why didn't you reach out?

29:28.224 --> 29:29.893
Don't you care if she leaves?

29:41.237 --> 29:42.238
She kissed you,

29:42.906 --> 29:45.074
and you're not reacting at all?

29:47.118 --> 29:48.745
So it really meant nothing to you?

29:55.293 --> 29:59.088
You said you'd never ask her out,
even if someone threatened you into it.

30:03.218 --> 30:05.178
Is this you keeping that promise?

30:14.145 --> 30:15.396
Love Shin Ji-sun that much?

30:22.195 --> 30:24.489
Please stop.
Don't ask him those questions.

30:27.867 --> 30:30.620
Do you really…

30:33.748 --> 30:35.333
not have

30:36.751 --> 30:37.877
any feelings

30:38.628 --> 30:39.921
for Cha Mu-hee

30:40.421 --> 30:41.339
whatsoever?

31:03.736 --> 31:05.363
You answer that question.

31:06.322 --> 31:07.824
You already know your answer.

31:32.223 --> 31:34.225
You know the answer
has already been decided,

31:35.143 --> 31:36.686
so why are you acting like this?

31:41.274 --> 31:44.402
Cha Mu-hee is a girl
who can never be loved.

31:45.695 --> 31:47.322
That was decided long ago.

32:11.596 --> 32:13.097
Didn't you go to bed early?

32:13.640 --> 32:15.016
I couldn't sleep.

32:15.099 --> 32:16.559
I'll just sleep on the plane.

32:18.937 --> 32:19.771
Yong-u.

32:20.438 --> 32:22.148
There are no auroras in Korea, right?

32:22.231 --> 32:24.400
Of course not.
It would be crazy to see one.

32:28.029 --> 32:30.615
Right. That would be crazy.

32:56.683 --> 32:57.517
Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

32:58.017 --> 33:00.228
I'll drive you to the airport.
Wanna get in?

33:21.916 --> 33:22.875
Mu-hee!

33:23.793 --> 33:24.752
Mr. Joo!

33:27.880 --> 33:30.008
Where are they even going?

34:01.080 --> 34:02.415
It's Cory Lane.

34:04.792 --> 34:06.335
He's a Canadian singer.

34:06.878 --> 34:08.838
A very famous singer-songwriter.

34:11.090 --> 34:11.924
I see.

34:12.425 --> 34:14.343
So he's super famous.

34:15.845 --> 34:17.972
It does feel like
I've heard this song before.

34:23.269 --> 34:25.396
Aren't you tired?

34:25.897 --> 34:27.732
You must've been up late drinking.

34:28.399 --> 34:29.358
I didn't drink.

34:30.109 --> 34:33.571
I got back early too. I didn't reach out
in case you had an early night.

34:35.865 --> 34:36.824
Oh.

34:37.658 --> 34:39.452
I see.

34:42.830 --> 34:43.790
I

34:45.249 --> 34:46.459
didn't sleep too well.

34:48.920 --> 34:50.880
I couldn't sleep
because it felt so unfair.

34:50.963 --> 34:52.715
How could you threaten me like that,

34:53.216 --> 34:56.052
act as though it never happened,
and then leave just like that?

34:56.552 --> 34:57.762
Is this about the gunshot?

35:00.807 --> 35:02.809
I mean, that was…

35:03.684 --> 35:05.436
Well, yes.

35:06.187 --> 35:09.565
I guess it was about as shocking
as getting shot.

35:11.609 --> 35:13.402
How can you shoot someone and walk off?

35:13.486 --> 35:17.323
You know I'm bad with directions,
yet you left me helplessly alone.

35:18.032 --> 35:19.408
That day,

35:19.992 --> 35:22.203
I told you that Do Ra-mi made me do it,

35:22.703 --> 35:25.706
but I couldn't smooth things over,
so I avoided you.

35:25.790 --> 35:27.834
I wasn't sure how to deal with it.

35:28.668 --> 35:30.628
You are the type to act on a whim,

35:30.711 --> 35:32.964
then deal with the fallout afterward.

35:33.589 --> 35:37.009
By pretending you never said anything
or by deflecting and running away.

35:38.886 --> 35:42.181
I came here to grab hold of you,
in case you might do that again.

35:43.182 --> 35:45.810
That's because you didn't seem
the least bit curious.

35:47.478 --> 35:48.938
I didn't sleep a wink either.

35:53.317 --> 35:54.402
Don't run this time.

35:58.197 --> 36:01.159
Because I'm giving it serious thought.

36:06.080 --> 36:08.833
I'm… the type
who needs to gather their thoughts

36:08.916 --> 36:11.752
before saying something,
especially if it's important.

36:17.258 --> 36:20.428
Which is why I'm going to do something
I vowed I never would.

36:22.430 --> 36:23.681
I'm gonna talk to Ji-sun.

36:28.728 --> 36:31.731
I don't want you to think I am pathetic.

36:46.621 --> 36:47.747
I agonized over it too…

36:50.208 --> 36:52.251
because this time…

36:58.257 --> 37:00.676
I didn't want to pretend
I never said what I said…

37:03.721 --> 37:05.223
or just run away.

37:26.285 --> 37:28.204
Take a nap on the way to the airport.

37:28.287 --> 37:29.789
You said you didn't get any sleep.

37:31.874 --> 37:33.125
I don't want to.

37:38.214 --> 37:40.883
This Mr. Cory Lane is a great singer.

37:45.304 --> 37:47.556
Mr. Joo Ho-jin,
you're catching the red-eye, right?

37:48.057 --> 37:50.268
What will you do until then? Sightsee?

37:50.768 --> 37:53.437
Ms. Cho is treating
the curling team to lunch.

37:55.690 --> 37:57.692
Right, the prince of the curling rink.

38:00.403 --> 38:01.988
Then what will you do after lunch?

38:02.571 --> 38:03.698
I haven't decided yet.

38:04.740 --> 38:05.574
But

38:06.993 --> 38:10.329
I'll call you once I decide.

38:12.039 --> 38:13.958
Though you'll be on the plane by then.

38:14.834 --> 38:18.629
Then I'll call you when you land
and let you know.

38:22.508 --> 38:23.426
Okay.

38:26.679 --> 38:28.222
You'd better call me.

38:40.568 --> 38:42.278
The weather is lovely.

38:45.323 --> 38:47.325
Isn't the song lovely too?

40:08.447 --> 40:09.281
There you are.

40:10.157 --> 40:11.575
Mu-hee, what are you doing?

40:11.659 --> 40:13.327
I'm listening to music.

40:13.828 --> 40:16.372
The song Mr. Joo and I listened to
on the drive over.

40:16.872 --> 40:20.418
It's by a singer he likes,
and he said the lyrics are great.

40:21.127 --> 40:21.961
Mu-hee.

40:22.461 --> 40:24.380
I'm not asking about the singer.

40:25.005 --> 40:26.048
Yong-u.

40:26.882 --> 40:29.093
Don't worry. I know what I'm doing.

40:36.684 --> 40:37.893
The wedding is off.

40:41.480 --> 40:43.441
Producer Shin broke up with her fiancé.

40:43.941 --> 40:46.026
I was there
when she told him on the phone.

40:52.950 --> 40:54.410
Is that right?

40:56.537 --> 40:58.914
Mr. Joo Ho-jin didn't seem to know.

41:00.207 --> 41:01.041
He will soon.

41:03.210 --> 41:04.712
I'm gonna talk to Ji-sun.

41:05.629 --> 41:09.508
It's harder to move on
when the person you like becomes single.

41:10.634 --> 41:13.304
Does Ho-jin like you enough
for it not to matter?

41:16.515 --> 41:17.516
Does he?

41:21.061 --> 41:23.230
If that's the case,
I was worried about nothing.

41:24.106 --> 41:26.942
He's not the type to be swayed
after telling you he wouldn't,

41:27.443 --> 41:28.944
so there's no need to worry.

41:35.034 --> 41:36.368
I'd better go.

41:39.538 --> 41:41.540
To be honest, I was too scared to ask.

41:42.625 --> 41:44.877
I'd better see him before they talk.

41:47.463 --> 41:48.464
Wait, Mu-hee!

42:18.494 --> 42:21.580
Even as I'm listening,
I have no idea what this song is about,

42:21.664 --> 42:23.666
so translate the lyrics for me next time.

42:24.291 --> 42:25.876
As we listen to it together.

42:36.136 --> 42:37.137
Here you are.

42:37.638 --> 42:39.265
Are you here to buy records?

42:40.474 --> 42:41.475
Yeah.

42:42.101 --> 42:43.769
I was thinking of buying some books.

42:44.270 --> 42:47.815
Can you recommend a few books
for me to read on the plane?

42:48.857 --> 42:49.858
Ji-sun.

42:50.568 --> 42:53.821
I was actually hoping
to talk to you after lunch.

42:54.780 --> 42:57.116
I'm glad I ran into you. We need to talk.

42:59.243 --> 43:00.244
Yeah.

43:00.744 --> 43:02.705
We should talk.

43:04.290 --> 43:05.165
Let's.

43:05.666 --> 43:06.500
This looks good.

43:07.042 --> 43:08.669
It's my treat,

43:09.420 --> 43:10.504
so anything expensive

43:11.255 --> 43:12.506
is off the table.

43:12.590 --> 43:14.466
Come on, Ms. Cho.

43:15.217 --> 43:18.012
-Can we have this steak?
-Just order noodles.

43:22.433 --> 43:25.311
Mu-hee? What are you doing here?
Did you miss your flight?

43:25.394 --> 43:27.313
You came here with Mr. Joo, right?

43:28.063 --> 43:28.897
Where is he?

43:30.649 --> 43:33.527
He's not here. He said
he was stopping by a bookstore.

43:39.408 --> 43:42.328
So you didn't know the wedding was off?

43:43.579 --> 43:45.414
Didn't Jin-suk call you?

43:48.208 --> 43:50.419
I thought you were
just pretending not to know.

43:52.129 --> 43:54.089
I did think the silence was strange.

43:54.173 --> 43:56.550
He always calls me when you two argue.

43:57.384 --> 44:00.763
I figured your argument was serious enough
to keep him from calling.

44:03.390 --> 44:07.645
I know Jin-suk must have bugged you a lot
whenever we had problems.

44:08.646 --> 44:11.315
I think I relied on you a lot too.

44:12.941 --> 44:15.778
Don't worry about smoothing things over
between us this time.

44:16.278 --> 44:19.156
Even better if you just pretend
not to know what's going on.

44:21.825 --> 44:23.452
You wanted to discuss this, right?

44:23.994 --> 44:26.288
-Let's join the others for lunch.
-Ji-sun.

45:56.587 --> 45:59.256
What a wonderful romance movie.
A perfect happy ending.

46:00.674 --> 46:01.759
What about me?

46:01.842 --> 46:05.929
You're, well… just a supporting character
who got in their way for a while?

46:06.013 --> 46:08.098
Or maybe the villain,
since you threatened him.

46:08.807 --> 46:11.143
What about the aurora? And the waterfall?

46:11.769 --> 46:13.270
The song we listened to together?

46:15.981 --> 46:19.985
Sure, there were scenes like that, too,
but that's how the story came to an end,

46:20.486 --> 46:23.822
so just erase them and move on.
Otherwise, it's just sad and pathetic.

46:24.573 --> 46:26.700
If you stay between those two,

46:27.326 --> 46:30.829
the ending you already know
will replay over and over in your mind.

46:31.413 --> 46:34.708
Isn't it sad to see them?
Isn't it painful? Agonizing?

46:35.959 --> 46:39.338
So just pretend you saw nothing,
know nothing, and it meant nothing.

46:42.299 --> 46:43.717
You're good at that.

46:44.802 --> 46:45.886
Just like back then.

46:54.019 --> 46:56.355
That's it. Just do what you did back then.

46:56.939 --> 46:59.775
Act like you saw nothing,
know nothing, and it meant nothing.

47:00.359 --> 47:01.360
Run away!

47:16.416 --> 47:17.543
I said I'm okay.

47:20.337 --> 47:21.421
What's the matter?

47:26.301 --> 47:27.302
You go ahead.

47:29.555 --> 47:30.597
Joo Ho-jin!

47:48.240 --> 47:49.449
I must have been mad.

47:51.159 --> 47:52.160
Ms. Cha Mu-hee!

47:57.165 --> 47:59.793
What are you doing here?
You should be on a plane by now.

48:02.713 --> 48:04.256
I'll catch a later flight.

48:04.339 --> 48:06.842
-Don't worry about me and go.
-Where's Yong-u?

48:07.843 --> 48:10.554
At the airport.
I should hurry over there now.

48:10.637 --> 48:11.763
Ms. Cha Mu-hee, wait.

48:15.517 --> 48:17.311
Let's go wash this off, then talk.

48:24.985 --> 48:27.279
I heard Producer Shin
isn't getting married.

48:29.907 --> 48:32.826
You heard, didn't you?
You were with her earlier.

48:34.453 --> 48:36.288
Yes, I heard.

48:42.127 --> 48:43.128
That's great.

48:45.297 --> 48:46.131
Sorry?

48:46.715 --> 48:50.385
Now you don't need to run away
or grab onto someone else to avoid her.

48:52.179 --> 48:53.764
I hope things work out this time.

48:59.603 --> 49:02.397
You missed your flight
and came here to tell me that?

49:04.191 --> 49:07.736
I need to get back to the airport.
You should go to her. She'll be waiting.

49:12.240 --> 49:14.993
I know you blurt things out
when you're flustered.

49:15.535 --> 49:19.289
Just stop… and say what you want to say,
instead of running away.

49:21.291 --> 49:23.543
That's it. Just do what you did back then.

49:24.169 --> 49:26.922
Act like you saw nothing,
know nothing, and it meant nothing.

49:27.005 --> 49:27.839
Run away!

49:29.758 --> 49:30.926
You…

49:33.887 --> 49:36.056
don't like me very much.

49:42.813 --> 49:44.940
That's why I came all this way.

49:46.274 --> 49:48.276
It hurt my pride. Got me fired up, even.

49:50.445 --> 49:52.948
Whatever it took,
I wanted to make you fall for me,

49:54.491 --> 49:58.120
but I didn't think it'd be possible
once you learned her wedding was off.

50:01.957 --> 50:05.669
So I missed my flight and rushed over here
to see you before you found out.

50:06.712 --> 50:07.754
You were…

50:09.881 --> 50:13.010
at least a little shaken by my threat,
weren't you?

50:18.306 --> 50:19.182
But…

50:23.478 --> 50:24.479
I was too late.

50:26.857 --> 50:30.235
I told you Do Ra-mi was like a hater
and that she talked about you.

50:34.948 --> 50:36.867
She kept taunting me.

50:39.327 --> 50:41.371
That it'd never work.
You'd never fall for me.

50:43.874 --> 50:45.292
And so…

50:48.086 --> 50:51.548
I'm going to just accept the fact
that you don't like me and give up.

50:53.717 --> 50:54.968
If I keep going…

50:57.054 --> 50:58.638
I'll look like such a fool.

51:06.813 --> 51:08.648
If I keep going, even now…

51:12.277 --> 51:14.321
I would feel so guilty.

51:21.703 --> 51:22.579
I understand.

51:25.082 --> 51:28.168
I'm sorry if I made you feel like a fool.

51:29.753 --> 51:30.837
Let's stop here.

51:35.842 --> 51:39.638
I sorted my thoughts
and made them clear to Ji-sun,

51:40.138 --> 51:41.515
so no need to feel guilty.

51:44.726 --> 51:46.353
Did your talk go well?

51:47.270 --> 51:48.480
Why should I tell you,

51:49.773 --> 51:51.525
given where we're at now?

51:54.861 --> 51:59.074
Seeing you wear your heart on your sleeve,
crying, laughing, changing,

52:00.450 --> 52:02.577
I was baffled but also fascinated.

52:04.538 --> 52:07.666
I came to worry about you,
to want to go along with what you wanted…

52:11.628 --> 52:13.088
and I wanted to take care of you.

52:14.631 --> 52:15.966
But now that I think about it,

52:16.967 --> 52:19.052
I was just being swayed by your emotions.

52:22.305 --> 52:23.723
It's best to end things here.

52:29.146 --> 52:30.063
This is

52:31.231 --> 52:34.151
the exact same situation
as the day we parted at the crosswalk.

52:36.903 --> 52:39.656
You were standing
on the other side of the train tracks…

52:42.367 --> 52:44.035
and I told you to go and get her.

52:48.248 --> 52:49.332
Just like that day…

52:54.129 --> 52:55.881
goodbye, Mr. Joo Ho-jin.

52:58.800 --> 53:01.219
Don't try to brush this off
like it was nothing.

53:03.763 --> 53:04.931
I feel very wronged.

53:08.685 --> 53:10.812
I was getting ready to cross the street

53:12.272 --> 53:13.440
to the person I like.

53:24.701 --> 53:27.370
Are you sure Do Ra-mi was wrong
and that you won?

53:29.247 --> 53:30.582
I hope that's the case.

53:31.458 --> 53:32.709
I did say I'd root for you.

54:46.241 --> 54:47.993
I thought I was gonna lose my mind.

54:48.076 --> 54:50.996
I was able to book a flight
with a stop in Japan, so we need to…

54:52.622 --> 54:53.498
Mu-hee.

54:57.502 --> 54:58.503
I…

55:01.089 --> 55:02.716
ruined everything.

55:22.777 --> 55:24.404
Did Ho-jin reject you again?

55:25.905 --> 55:26.948
Come here.

55:29.367 --> 55:30.577
Who does he think he is?

55:31.536 --> 55:32.787
He's not all that.

56:10.950 --> 56:12.911
The reason I mediated between you two

56:13.411 --> 56:14.913
wasn't because Jin-suk bugged me

56:15.413 --> 56:16.956
or because you relied on me.

56:17.832 --> 56:19.876
As long as your relationship was intact,

56:20.377 --> 56:24.047
I could ensure
that my world was safe and peaceful.

56:27.759 --> 56:31.596
But a certain someone
started shaking up my world.

56:33.973 --> 56:38.186
I tried pushing her away, afraid the world
I'd protected would break and shatter,

56:39.854 --> 56:42.357
but light shone in
through the cracks she made.

57:30.488 --> 57:31.573
Are you okay?

57:40.999 --> 57:42.000
Are you okay?

57:43.376 --> 57:45.211
You haven't budged since earlier.

57:47.714 --> 57:48.923
Are you unwell?

58:20.288 --> 58:21.748
TWO WEEKS LATER, KOREA

58:22.582 --> 58:26.753
As you asked, I didn't tell
the production crew you're in Korea.

58:28.296 --> 58:30.507
As for Ms. Cha Mu-hee,

58:30.590 --> 58:34.636
she'll be attending a concert
sponsored by an advertiser.

58:36.846 --> 58:39.015
I know you didn't ask me to,

58:39.098 --> 58:41.684
but I thought
I'd check her schedule just in case.

58:42.185 --> 58:43.645
A concert?

58:45.313 --> 58:47.649
She went to a concert
without a care in the world?

58:49.317 --> 58:51.069
After what she did to me?

59:09.587 --> 59:11.339
Is the woman next to me an actress?

59:12.590 --> 59:13.424
Pardon?

59:14.926 --> 59:16.261
Yes, she's an actress.

59:16.844 --> 59:19.722
Mr. Kim, I wonder if you've heard of her.

59:20.515 --> 59:22.100
She's Do Ra-mi, the--

59:22.183 --> 59:23.059
Cha Mu-hee?

59:23.142 --> 59:24.852
Yes, that was her name.

59:25.979 --> 59:27.272
Wait, you know her name?

59:27.355 --> 59:29.691
-Of course I know Cha Mu-hee.
-Oh, really?

59:35.113 --> 59:36.322
I think today's concert

59:36.948 --> 59:38.283
will be very interesting.

59:45.081 --> 59:46.457
Hello.

01:00:08.938 --> 01:00:10.023
"Hello."

01:00:10.857 --> 01:00:14.402
"I am Roberto Vancini,
the Ambassador of Italy to Korea."

01:00:15.236 --> 01:00:18.865
"Thank you for attending this concert
hosted by the Italian Embassy,

01:00:18.948 --> 01:00:23.828
commemorating the 140th anniversary
of Korea-Italy diplomatic relations."

01:00:36.257 --> 01:00:39.135
"I hope tonight's musical journey to Italy

01:00:39.218 --> 01:00:43.431
becomes a beautiful
and delightful memory for you."

01:00:43.514 --> 01:00:44.515
"Thank you."

01:01:32.772 --> 01:01:35.733
CAN THIS LOVE BE TRANSLATED?

01:03:55.998 --> 01:04:01.003
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
